 {r}←{leftRight}FormatTableInMarkdown n;curPos;ind;cells;markdown;newCursorCol
⍝ Extracts the table the cursor is in from the Markdown, has it formatted by `FormatTable`
⍝ and injects the result back into the Markdown.
⍝ The formatted table as well as the index into the Markdown items is returned.
⍝ If the cursor is not in a table nothing happens and `⍬ ⍬` is returned.
⍝ If the optional `⍺` is provided, a new column is added. `⍺` must be either "left" or "right".
⍝ The new column is added either to the left or the right of the cursor.
 r←⍬ ⍬
 curPos←¯1+0 0⊃n.Markdown.SelText                               ⍝ Where is the cursor?
 :If n CursorIsInTable curPos
 :AndIf 0<≢ind←GetTableRows curPos n.Markdown.Text              ⍝ The rows the table consists of
     :If 0=⎕NC'leftRight'
         (cells markdown newCursorCol)←FormatTable(n.Markdown.Text[ind])(ind⍳curPos)(¯1+0 1⊃n.Markdown.SelText)
     :Else
         (cells markdown newCursorCol)←leftRight FormatTable(n.Markdown.Text[ind])(ind⍳curPos)(¯1+0 1⊃n.Markdown.SelText)
     :EndIf
 :AndIf ⍬≢cells                                                 ⍝ Was it a table after all?
     :If n.Markdown.Text[ind]≢markdown
         ##.SaveTextForUndo n
         ##.∆SKIP_SAVE_FOR_UNDO←1
         n.Markdown.Text[ind]←markdown
         n.Markdown.SelText←2⍴⊂(1+curPos),newCursorCol
     :EndIf
     r←cells ind
 :EndIf
⍝Done
